		},
		{
			"id": "s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar I - Hypotheses|Hypotheses index]]**",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Cellular energy and mitochondrial hypotheses]]**\n*theory* - 6 sources\n\nThe proposal that cellular energy metabolism contributes to bipolar disorder, and what the supporting evidence can bear.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Circadian and social rhythm hypotheses]]**\n*theory* - 5 sources\n\nThe proposal that rhythm disruption links life events to mood episodes, together with the evidence and its limits.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Dopamine hypothesis in bipolar disorder]]**\n*theory* - 4 sources\n\nState-dependent dopamine findings, the pharmacological clues that complicate a single-direction account, and the boundary between group evidence and individual inference.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1064,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 266,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Inflammation and immune hypotheses in bipolar disorder]]**\n*theory* - 5 sources\n\nImmune markers in bipolar disorder, the inflammation-depression model they borrow from, and the interpretation limits.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1390,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Evidence and treatment",
			"x": 840,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1870
		},
		{
			"id": "s2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar I - Evidence and treatment|Evidence and treatment index]]**",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar MRI findings and their limits]]**\n*method* - 3 sources\n\nWhat consortium imaging studies show in bipolar disorder, the confounds they cannot remove, and why they do not classify individuals.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar genetics and polygenic risk]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nPolygenic architecture in bipolar disorder, genetic sharing with other conditions, and why loci are not mechanisms or diagnoses.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar psychotherapy evidence]]**\n*framework* - 3 sources\n\nWhat adjunctive psychotherapy trials in bipolar disorder test, what they find for recurrence and symptoms, and why component estimates are averages.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1064,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Lithium mechanisms and uncertainty]]**\n*mechanism* - 3 sources\n\nLithium's signalling targets, why its recurrence-prevention mechanism stays unresolved, and how narrow-window monitoring is a class property.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1342,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Phase-specific bipolar treatment evidence]]**\n*framework* - 4 sources\n\nWhy bipolar treatment evidence is organised by phase, how guidelines attach strength to evidence, and the boundaries of what trials measure.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1620,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychoeducation and social rhythms]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nPsychoeducation and social rhythm components, the circadian machinery they target, and the status of social zeitgeber theory.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1922,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
